  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 204 PM MST Fri Nov 6 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nA weak upper-level ridge is over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will allow temperatures to warm up today. \nDue to a strong surface pressure gradient and strong low-level winds \nit will be windy across North-central Montana this afternoon through \nearly Saturday morning with the strongest winds along the Rocky \nMountain Front and plains west of I-15. This afternoon it will be \nmostly dry. On Saturday the upper-level ridge strengthens and the \nstrong winds aloft move higher into the atmosphere. This results in \nwarm and dry weather for the area with strong winds ending by mid-\nmorning on Saturday. On Saturday it will be dry.\n\nOn Sunday the upper-level ridge breaks down. This combined with \nstrong low-level and mid-level winds will bring another day of windy \nconditions to North-central Montana. The strongest winds will be \nalong the Rocky Mountain Front. On Sunday it will be dry. On Monday \nan upper-level ridge moves back over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will continue the warm and dry conditions \nfor the area. Tuesday through Thursday the upper-level ridge remains \nover North-central Montana. This will keep warm and dry weather for \nthe area Tuesday through Thursday. Tuesday through Thursday it will \nalso be breezy across North-central Montana. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nFor winds this afternoon into early Saturday morning there is a 50 -\n80% chance for wind gusts of 70 mph or greater along the Rocky \nMountain Front. For winds along the plains west of I-15 this \nafternoon into Sunday morning there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind \ngusts of 55 mph along the plains west of I-15. As a result a High \nWind Warning was issued for those areas through 9 am Saturday. \nAcross most of the rest of North-central Montana there is a 30 - 60% \nchance for wind gusts of 55 mph or greater.\n\nOn Sunday along the Hi-line east of I-15 and in the lower-elevations \nof Cascade County there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 55 \nmph or greater. On Sunday along the Rocky Mountain Front there is a \n50 - 80% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph or greater. On Sunday \nacross the plains west of I-15 there is a 40 - 80% chance for wind \ngusts of 70 mph or greater. As a result during the day on Sunday a \nHigh Wind Watch is in effect for the Hi-Line through Hill County,\nthe Rocky Mountain Front, and the lower-elevations of Cascade \nCounty. -IG",
